## What the agent does

For each disease the agent receives a rendered observation (target, druggability, current
stage, budget remaining, recent action history, sub-agent messages) and must emit a JSON
action choosing one of **13 tools**:

| Category | Tools |
|---|---|
| Targeting | `select_target` |
| Search | `search_compounds`, `search_literature` |
| Assays | `predict_affinity`, `evaluate_admet` |
| Optimization | `modify_molecule`, `synthesize`, `validate_compound` |
| Process | `advance_stage`, `abandon_compound`, `pause_and_review_all` |
| Sub-agents | `delegate_to_subagent`, `request_subagent_summary` |

Each call has a **credit cost**, **assay noise**, and a **stage-gated availability**. The
campaign ends when the agent runs out of budget, hits 50 steps, or successfully validates
a compound through all 4 stages.

Critically, the data layer is **cached targets, live tools**: target metadata and
known-drug SMILES are baked into the dataset (so training is reproducible and cheap),
but ChEMBL similarity / PubMed retrieval can be proxied through `LiveAPIProvider` so the
agent really learns *what* to query rather than memorizing a fixed tool API.

