## The reward — smooth, single-step, multi-objective

A core design choice: every reward component is a **smooth, bounded function** with a
clear physical meaning, so GRPO sees a dense signal instead of a sparse end-of-episode
spike.

| Component | Form | Intuition |
|-----------|------|-----------|
| `terminal_compound` | `sigmoid(w_p · (pIC50 − 6)) · exp(−herg) · (0.5 + 0.5·ro5_pass) · w_n / (1 + dup_count)` | Potency × safety × drug-likeness × novelty, with a hard hERG/PAINS floor that zeroes the term. |
| `process` | `mean(info_gain / (1 + log1p(cost)))` over the last 5 actions | Pay for queries that *teach* you something. |
| `strategy` | `0.5·(1 − exp(−N_compounds/3)) + 0.5·(stage_idx / (S−1))` | Balance breadth and progress. |
| `reasoning_depth` | `tanh(unique_concepts/6) · tanh(mean_len/200)` | Reward distinct, sufficiently-developed chains of thought (parsed from the agent's text). |
| `budget_efficiency` | `(remaining/total)^0.7` | Don't burn the budget for nothing. |
| `oversight_penalty` | `1 − exp(−ignored)` | Penalty for ignoring sub-agent flags (toxicologist, etc.). |
| `stage_progression` | `cleared / 4` | Linear credit for actually advancing through gates. |

The aggregator is a single weighted sum minus the oversight penalty; all weights live in
[`config/defaults.yaml`](config/defaults.yaml) and can be overridden via a layered YAML.
This made it easy to ablate: e.g. zero out `process` and watch the policy collapse into
a "spam validate_compound" failure mode.

